{"agent_id":"pp3g-dK8V-revise-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-230b","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:49:47.518169091Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e5970fc-f7ae-46fd-bd36-44501b5d5c35","comment_uuid":"dac003bd-316c-4b03-9db2-e507fffe81ab","author":"pp3g-dK8V-revise-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-230b","content":"Plan: Revise the #175 design to address ALL reviewer findings (r1 #176: B1-B3, F4-F13; r2 #177: 5 fixes; r3 #178: R1-R3). Evidence verified this session: (a) fetched upstream v1.18.12 source — aiskd.ts (235 lines) has a SECOND wrapSSE guard copy (L29, plain Error, NO headerTimeout) consumed only by v2 plugin AISDK hooks; v2 SessionRunner (runner-llm.ts) uses LLMClient/@opencode-ai/llm routes, NOT aiskd; harness logs prove v1 processor+llm is the live path for 'opencode run'; (b) retry.ts verified: meta.attempt is 1-based RETRY count (delay(1)=2000ms), policy() unbounded, retry-after honored to RETRY_MAX_DELAY, upstream test waits >10min; (c) message-v2.ts fromError codes: ProviderResponseStreamError / ProviderHeaderTimeoutError / ECONNRESET — the bounded error-class key; (d) build.ts defines OPENCODE_VERSION/OPENCODE_CHANNEL (L192-199), root packageManager=bun@1.3.14, root postinstall=fix-node-pty, --skip-embed-web-ui exists; (e) LIVE STATE: binary now 1.18.13 (upgraded AGAIN), #179 stopgap appears applied — both guard copies byte-patched (dy + or, if(false)return + /*XXX*/ filler), autoupdate:false now set; production config timeout=3600000, no bodyIdleTimeout yet. Deliverable: revised design (Option A' idle-progress deadline, error-class-scoped retry budget, both-copy patch, turn-level guard, atomic install, fork-identity marker, expanded matrix) + change-log vs #175, posted as --kind result to #180. DESIGN-ONLY: no code/binary changes.","created_at":"2026-08-05T22:49:47.508070294Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:yCnB3Tge2Cf5fii5l09gwZzIGgjawvUvgOlEO8nFj0Y","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJQfYmJw/yj35gN7WfEJDtoGIQNsjZ/81zm51A0IlrnsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAcV/vHiXbmshGrCS2Xvrs3KFNbRXtbyq14g36/BDq6kZPAGESTFIN5mhnMpheHZIf+mgIE2wCaVaHCwepA4P0Cg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:yCnB3Tge2Cf5fii5l09gwZzIGgjawvUvgOlEO8nFj0Y","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJQfYmJw/yj35gN7WfEJDtoGIQNsjZ/81zm51A0IlrnsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBfZydvPJvHMr0934S+RwpaRg+7ZinXZoXEDM5AZIErF2I+PX4jypP/dCw6L3MUreyMxnPhMn4DyItdbmMZWQws="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-dK8V-revise-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-230b","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:52:48.675262361Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e5970fc-f7ae-46fd-bd36-44501b5d5c35","comment_uuid":"d9d1f7e7-9249-435b-98c0-4bd281351073","author":"pp3g-dK8V-revise-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-230b","content":"# DESIGN (REVISED): Durable opencode silent-hang fix (#154) — round 2\n\n**Sub-issue**: #180 (round 2 of #175) · **Parent**: #154 · **Epic**: #156\n**Designer**: Builder pp3g-dK8V (design-only task; no code or binary changes made)\n**Inputs**: #175 baseline design; reviewer verdicts r1 hy3 (#176: B1/B2/B3, F4–F13), r2 luna (#177: 5 fixes), r3 big-pickle (#178: R1/R2/R3); upstream source @ v1.18.12 re-fetched and verified this session; live machine state re-verified this session.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Current state (re-verified this session — updated since #175)\n\nThe machine state has moved since both #175 (§0) and the reviews:\n\n- **Installed binary is now `1.18.13`** (mtime `2026-08-05 22:47:19`, size `180,381,824`) — upgraded *again* after the reviews' \"1.18.12\" snapshot. The reviews' §0 evidence is already stale; any design must not assume a fixed installed version.\n- **The #179 stopgap appears to be applied** (issue #179 created today 22:42, binary mtime 22:47): both guard copies in the live binary are byte-patched — `function dy` (v1 `provider.ts` path) and `function or` (v2 AISDK path) both contain `if(false)return $;/*XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX*/` (same-length replacement, filler comment) — and **`\"autoupdate\": false` is now present** in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` (verified by parse).\n- **Production config** (verified): `chunkTimeout=300000`, `headerTimeout=300000`, `timeout=3600000` on both `opencode` and `opencode-go`; **no** `bodyIdleTimeout` / `bodyTimeout` yet.\n- Consequence: the box currently has *ephemeral* protection (the #145-style byte patch, both copies) plus self-update disabled. It is **not** the durable fix: any manual npm upgrade wipes the byte patch. The durable fork remains the outstanding work, and the two-copy coverage of the byte patch is the coverage baseline the source patch must match.\n\n**Design-only constraint**: this document changes no files and no binaries; §6 \"step 0\" interim actions are implementation steps, not actions taken here.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Fork strategy (approved by all three reviewers — kept with one update)\n\n1. **Canonical upstream**: `anomalyco/opencode` (formerly `sst/opencode`; the old name is a 301 redirect to the same repo — verified by all three reviewers).\n2. **Pin**: the fork pins the **installed version at implementation time** — today that is `v1.18.13`. `provider.ts` is byte-identical between v1.18.11/v1.18.12 (verified by reviewers and this session); **re-verify byte-identity of `provider.ts` AND `aiskd.ts` at the chosen pin before building**. Pinning the installed version keeps `opencode --version` coherent with the npm package (`opencode-ai@1.18.13`).\n3. **Patch as a committed fork divergence** (one commit per file), keeping a clean rebase path against upstream tags — the crosslink-fork pattern in `.crosslink/knowledge/crosslink-fork.md`.\n4. **Upgrade survival** (unchanged from #175, reviewer-approved): (a) launch-chain indirection — fork binary at `~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe`, wrapper `REAL` pointed at it; (b) `autoupdate: false` — **now already set** (verified); (c) **new: fork-identity marker + launch-time drift detection** (§6.4) so a silent wipe becomes a hard failure instead of a silent regression.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Exact patches — BOTH guard copies (B1)\n\n### 2.1 Why both copies (evidence)\n\nThe shipped binary contains **two independent implementations** of the SSE wrapper:\n\n- **v1**: `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` `wrapSSE` (L37–82, guard at L40) → `ProviderError.ResponseStreamError`, paired with `headerTimeout` in the `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper (L1738–1767).\n- **v2**: `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` `wrapSSE` (L26–72, guard at L29) → raises a **plain `Error`** (not `ProviderError.ResponseStreamError`), **no `headerTimeout` at all**; wired in `prepareOptions` fetch wrapper (L82–119).\n\nThe #145 byte patch neutralised **both** (verified live: `dy` + `or` both patched). A source patch that covers one is a coverage regression relative to the interim patch it supersedes. Therefore:\n\n**Decision: patch BOTH files** (defense-in-depth, coverage parity with #145), and record the reachability analysis below as an explicit assumption re-checked on every rebase.\n\n**Reachability evidence for the v2 copy** (why patching it is cheap insurance rather than guesswork):\n1. `opencode run` (the CLI the `claude` wrapper invokes) executes the **v1** `SessionProcessor` → `llm.ts` → `provider.ts`. Harness logs (`/tmp/opencode-hang-test/run-mode1.out`) contain v1-only log lines: `message=process session.id=...` (processor.ts) and `message=\"llm runtime selected\" llm.runtime=ai-sdk` (llm.ts:271).\n2. #144's four `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries can only be emitted by v1 — v2 `aiskd.ts` has no `headerTimeout` code (verified L82–119). Suggestive, not conclusive, that v1 is the live path — but combined with (1) it is strong.\n3. The **v2 `SessionRunner`** (`packages/core/src/session/runner/llm.ts`) uses `LLMClient` (`llm.stream(request)` on `@opencode-ai/llm` route protocols); its model resolver (`runner/model.ts`) resolves via `OpenAIResponses.route` / `AnthropicMessages.route` / `OpenAICompatibleChat.route` — **neither touches `aiskd.ts`**.\n4. `aiskd.ts` is consumed only through the **v2 plugin AISDK hooks** (`packages/plugin/src/v2/effect/aisdk.ts`, `packages/plugin/src/v2/promise/aisdk.ts`). None of our configured providers (`opencode-go` = npm `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` via v1 provider options) register a language model through those hooks.\n\n**Rebase re-check (mandatory, codified in §6.5)**: after every upstream rebase, grep-count the content-type guard in both files — must be 0 in each — and grep-count the new marker functions/strings (must be ≥1 in each).\n\n### 2.2 Patch A — `provider.ts` (v1)\n\n**Hunk 1 — `wrapSSE` region (L35–82): add `wrapBodyIdle`.** Same `pull()` shape as `wrapSSE` (backpressure preserved, F6) with a hardened timer/controller lifecycle (F7) and its own error message/knob:\n\n```diff\n const OPENAI_HEADER_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT = 300_000\n+// NEW: idle-progress deadline for non-SSE response bodies (Option A').\n+// The timer resets on every chunk, so a slow-but-progressing body is never\n+// aborted (hy3 F2 preserved); only a body that stalls >= ms between chunks is.\n+// Optional absoluteMs is a belt-and-braces total cap (opt-in, default off).\n+function wrapBodyIdle(res: Response, ms: number, ctl: AbortController, absoluteMs?: number) {\n+  if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res\n+  if (!res.body) return res\n+  const reader = res.body.getReader()\n+  let settled = false\n+  let absoluteId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined\n+  const body = new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({\n+    async pull(ctrl) {\n+      if (settled) return\n+      const part = await new Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof reader.read>>>((resolve, reject) => {\n+        const id = setTimeout(() => {\n+          if (settled) return\n+          settled = true\n+          const err = new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read timed out\")\n+          ctl.abort(err)\n+          void reader.cancel(err).catch(() => {})\n+          reject(err)\n+        }, ms)\n+        reader.read().then(\n+          (part) => {\n+            clearTimeout(id)\n+            resolve(part)\n+          },\n+          (err) => {\n+            clearTimeout(id)\n+            reject(err)\n+          },\n+        )\n+      })\n+      if (settled) return\n+      if (part.done) {\n+        settled = true\n+        if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n+        ctrl.close()\n+        return\n+      }\n+      ctrl.enqueue(part.value)\n+    },\n+    async cancel(reason) {\n+      if (settled) return\n+      settled = true\n+      if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n+      ctl.abort(reason)\n+      await reader.cancel(reason).catch(() => {})\n+    },\n+  })\n+  if (typeof absoluteMs === \"number\" && absoluteMs > 0) {\n+    absoluteId = setTimeout(() => {\n+      if (settled) return\n+      settled = true\n+      const err = new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read deadline exceeded\")\n+      ctl.abort(err)\n+      void reader.cancel(err).catch(() => {})\n+    }, absoluteMs)\n+  }\n+  return new Response(body, {\n+    headers: new Headers(res.headers),\n+    status: res.status,\n+    statusText: res.statusText,\n+  })\n+}\n```\n\nLifecycle notes (F7): `settled` guard prevents `ctrl.close()` after `ctrl.error()`; `clearTimeout` runs on `done` and in `cancel()`; the cancel promise gets `.catch(() => {})`; the absolute-cap timer is cleared on `done`/`cancel`. `wrapSSE` itself is left byte-identical except it may reuse the same hardened `settled` guard for consistency (optional, non-behavioral).\n\n**Hunk 2 — `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper (L1738–1767): opt-in `bodyIdleTimeout`, dispatcher:**\n\n```diff\n         const customFetch = options[\"fetch\"]\n         const chunkTimeout = options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         const headerTimeout = options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        const bodyIdleTimeout = options[\"bodyIdleTimeout\"]\n+        const bodyAbsoluteTimeout = options[\"bodyAbsoluteTimeout\"]\n         delete options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         delete options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        delete options[\"bodyIdleTimeout\"]\n+        delete options[\"bodyAbsoluteTimeout\"]\n\n         options[\"fetch\"] = async (input: any, init?: BunFetchRequestInit) => {\n           const fetchFn = customFetch ?? fetch\n           const opts = init ?? {}\n           const chunkAbortCtl = typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n+          const bodyIdleAbortCtl =\n+            typeof bodyIdleTimeout === \"number\" && bodyIdleTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n           const headerTimeoutMs = headerTimeout === false ? undefined : headerTimeout\n           const headerTimeoutCtl = typeof headerTimeoutMs === \"number\" ? timeoutController(headerTimeoutMs) : undefined\n           const signals: AbortSignal[] = []\n\n           if (opts.signal) signals.push(opts.signal)\n           if (chunkAbortCtl) signals.push(chunkAbortCtl.signal)\n+          if (bodyIdleAbortCtl) signals.push(bodyIdleAbortCtl.signal)\n           if (headerTimeoutCtl) signals.push(headerTimeoutCtl.signal)\n           if (options[\"timeout\"] !== undefined && options[\"timeout\"] !== null && options[\"timeout\"] !== false)\n             signals.push(AbortSignal.timeout(options[\"timeout\"]))\n\n           const combined = signals.length === 0 ? null : signals.length === 1 ? signals[0] : AbortSignal.any(signals)\n           if (combined) opts.signal = combined\n\n           const res = await fetchFn(input, {\n             ...opts,\n             // @ts-ignore see here: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/16682\n             timeout: false,\n           }).finally(() => headerTimeoutCtl?.clear())\n\n-          if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n-          return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          const isSSE = res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")\n+          if (isSSE) {\n+            if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n+            return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          }\n+          if (!bodyIdleAbortCtl) return res\n+          return wrapBodyIdle(res, bodyIdleTimeout, bodyIdleAbortCtl, bodyAbsoluteTimeout)\n         }\n```\n\n**F8 (opt-in)**: `bodyIdleTimeout` is opt-in exactly like `chunkTimeout` (`false`/`0`/absent → no wrapping). It does **not** default ON, so compressed bodies, non-chat traffic, and providers that never configured it are untouched until the operator opts in via provider options. The durable config change (production `opencode` + `opencode-go` providers) adds `bodyIdleTimeout: 600000`. Dispatcher note: content-type absent → treated as non-SSE → `bodyIdleTimeout` applies when configured (r2's absent-content-type coverage).\n\n### 2.3 Patch B — `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` (v2)\n\nSame dispatcher + `wrapBodyIdle`, adapted to the file's conventions (plain `Error` is the file's existing style — see note):\n\n**Hunk 3 — `wrapSSE` region (L26–72): add `wrapBodyIdle`** — identical structure to Patch A hunk 1, except the error is `new Error(\"Body read timed out\")` (matching the file's existing `new Error(\"SSE read timed out\")` at L36) with the same `settled` guard / `clearTimeout` / `.catch` hardening.\n\n**Hunk 4 — `prepareOptions` fetch wrapper (L82–119):**\n\n```diff\n   const customFetch = options.fetch\n   const chunkTimeout = options.chunkTimeout\n+  const bodyIdleTimeout = options.bodyIdleTimeout\n+  const bodyAbsoluteTimeout = options.bodyAbsoluteTimeout\n   delete options.chunkTimeout\n+  delete options.bodyIdleTimeout\n+  delete options.bodyAbsoluteTimeout\n   options.fetch = async (input, init) => {\n     const opts = { ...(init ?? {}) }\n     const signals = [\n       opts.signal,\n       typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined,\n+      typeof bodyIdleTimeout === \"number\" && bodyIdleTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined,\n       options.timeout !== undefined && options.timeout !== null && options.timeout !== false\n         ? AbortSignal.timeout(options.timeout)\n         : undefined,\n     ].filter((item): item is AbortSignal | AbortController => Boolean(item))\n     const chunkAbortCtl = signals.find((item): item is AbortController => item instanceof AbortController)\n     const abortSignals = signals.map((item) => (item instanceof AbortController ? item.signal : item))\n     if (abortSignals.length === 1) opts.signal = abortSignals[0]\n     if (abortSignals.length > 1) opts.signal = AbortSignal.any(abortSignals)\n+    // (existing openai/azure/bedrock request-body mutation block unchanged)\n     const res = await (typeof customFetch === \"function\" ? customFetch : fetch)(input, {\n       ...opts,\n       timeout: false,\n     })\n-    if (!chunkAbortCtl || typeof chunkTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n-    return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+    const isSSE = res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")\n+    if (isSSE) {\n+      if (!chunkAbortCtl || typeof chunkTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n+      return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+    }\n+    if (!bodyIdleAbortCtl || typeof bodyIdleTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n+    return wrapBodyIdle(res, bodyIdleTimeout, bodyIdleAbortCtl, bodyAbsoluteTimeout)\n   }\n```\n\n*(Hunk 4 requires the controller selection to keep both controllers; the patch text must be finalised against the exact source at implementation — the fetched v1.18.12 source is the base and is included in the fork.)*\n\n**v2 error-class note (B1)**: `aiskd.ts` raises a plain `Error`, which `MessageV2.fromError` would route to `UnknownError` — but that mapping is on the **v1** path. The v2 plugin AISDK path does not route through `MessageV2.fromError`; the v2 `SessionRunner` uses `LLMError` from `@opencode-ai/llm`. So the plain-`Error` distinction does not affect the v1 retry analysis, and the v2 patch's job is purely to *terminate* a hang (guard removal + deadline). **Documented as an explicit v2-path limitation**: the v2 AISDK hook path has no `headerTimeout`; if a v2 plugin path is ever adopted, a header timeout must be added separately. This is re-checked on every rebase (§6.5).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Non-SSE deadline — Option A' (idle-progress) adopted (B2)\n\n### 3.1 Decision\n\n**Replace the #175 Option B (total-completion deadline) with Option A': a distinct, longer per-chunk idle-progress deadline for the non-SSE branch.**\n\n- `bodyIdleTimeout` (default when configured: **600_000 ms = 10 min**), resetting on every chunk — mechanically identical to `wrapSSE`'s proven per-read timer.\n- Optional `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` = **3_300_000 ms = 55 min** (slightly under the 1 h request `timeout`) as an opt-in belt-and-braces total cap. **Default OFF** — see trade-off.\n\n### 3.2 Why A' dominates both A and B\n\n| | Option A (relax guard → reuse `chunkTimeout`) | Option B (#175: total-completion `bodyTimeout`) | **Option A' (adopted)** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Non-SSE hang detection | after chunkTimeout idle | after bodyTimeout *wall-clock* | after bodyIdleTimeout idle |\n| Slow-but-progressing non-SSE body (hy3 F2) | **false-aborted** on any gap > chunkTimeout | preserved (timer only on done) | **preserved** (timer resets per chunk) |\n| Long *streaming* response labelled non-SSE (Bedrock eventstream, ndjson, text/plain) making steady progress | false-aborted on gap > chunkTimeout | **false-aborted** once wall-clock > bodyTimeout — **new false-abort class** | preserved (steady progress resets idle) |\n| Detection latency (dead body, 3-POST budget) | ~chunkTimeout × attempts (5 min × 3 = 15 min at prod settings) | bodyTimeout × attempts (30 min × 3 = **90 min**) | bodyIdleTimeout × attempts (10 min × 3 = **30 min**) |\n| Regression risk | HIGH (untested slow-non-SSE) | MEDIUM (new long-stream false-abort) | LOW (idle semantics for both) |\n\nThe #175 rationale that \"`wrapBody` starts ONE timer and clears it only on `done`; it cannot false-fire on a slow-but-steady body\" is **also true of an idle timer** — an idle timer resets on every chunk, so slow-but-progressing bodies never trip it. The table in #175 mis-scored Option A' by charging the *idle mechanism* with a false-abort risk that only exists because `chunkTimeout` is tuned for SSE — not because idle timing is the wrong shape. That is the core of r1's B2.\n\n### 3.3 Numeric justification vs `timeout: 3600000` and the retry budget (B3)\n\nProduction request `timeout` = 3_600_000 ms (1 h). Retry budget (§4) = **≤3 POSTs** (`RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2`).\n\n- **Dead-body detection latency (worst case)**: `bodyIdleTimeout × max POSTs` = 600_000 × 3 = **1_800_000 ms (30 min)** to terminal ERROR + idle status. vs Option B's 90 min; vs the interim #145 patch's 300 s; vs the **10.9 h** production hang (#142/OZWZ). The flag stops lying as RUNNING within 30 min worst-case.\n- **Chain inequality** (r1's requirement): `bodyIdleTimeout × attempts` (30 min) **<** request `timeout` (60 min) **<** operator/kickoff timeout (task-matched; for long agents the operator timeout is ≥ 60 min; for shorter agents the operator timeout fires first as the outer net — the point is the *visible ERROR* now surfaces at ≤ 30 min regardless, well before any outer kill).\n- **Backoff**: `RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY × 2^(attempt-1)` = 2 s + 4 s across 2 retries — negligible against the 30-min ceiling.\n- Per-attempt ceiling: each POST is bounded by the *first* of {bodyIdleTimeout fire (10 min idle), bodyAbsoluteTimeout if set (55 min), request timeout (60 min)} — in every realistic hang the idle timer fires first.\n\n### 3.4 Documented false-abort class of Option B (now rejected)\n\nA total-completion deadline on the non-SSE branch kills a legitimately long *streaming* response that keeps producing past the wall-clock cap. `non-SSE content-type` is not a synonym for `non-streaming body`: Bedrock's `application/vnd.amazon.eventstream` (upstream #26487's exact case), ndjson, and `text/plain` streaming all land in the non-SSE branch. A total-completion deadline is the correct guard only for single-shot bodies, and the content-type dispatcher cannot tell the two apart. **Option A' does not have this class** — steady progress resets the idle timer; only a body that stalls ≥ 10 min is aborted. The opt-in absolute cap re-introduces a *bounded* version of this class (55-min steady stream killed) — which is why it is **opt-in, default OFF**, documented as the explicit price of belt-and-braces.\n\n### 3.5 Trade-off kept\n\nA non-SSE body that legitimately pauses > 10 min between chunks is now aborted (previously unbounded). Acceptable and configurable via `bodyIdleTimeout`; it is the price of killing the 10.9 h signature. `chunkTimeout`/`headerTimeout` semantics unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Error surfacing + retry budget (B3, F4, R1, F9)\n\n### 4.1 Root cause (re-verified in v1.18.12 source)\n\n`SessionRetry.policy()` (retry.ts:176–199) is `Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata` with **no recurs cap**; `meta.attempt` is a **1-based RETRY count** (verified: `delay(attempt)` = `RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY × 2^(attempt-1)`, retry.ts:65 — attempt 1 → 2000 ms, matching the observed first-retry gap in #145). `ResponseStreamError` → `APIError { isRetryable: true, metadata.code: \"ProviderResponseStreamError\" }` (message-v2.ts:665); `HeaderTimeoutError` → code `\"ProviderHeaderTimeoutError\"` (message-v2.ts:653); `ECONNRESET` → code `\"ECONNRESET\"` (message-v2.ts:625). `halt()` (processor.ts:599) publishes ERROR + `Session.Event.Error` + idle — reachable only when the schedule gives up.\n\n### 4.2 Design\n\n1. **Per-attempt retry logging at the retry boundary (F4 — zero policy risk, fixes operator blindness independently of the cap).** Inside `SessionRetry.policy()`'s step (retry.ts:186–196), where `retry`/`wait`/`now` are already computed, before/after `opts.set(...)`:\n   ```ts\n   yield* Effect.logWarning(\"retry\", {\n     provider: opts.provider,\n     attempt: meta.attempt,                    // 1-based retry count\n     code: SessionV1.APIError.isInstance(error) ? error.data.metadata?.code ?? error.data.message : String(error),\n     nextDelay: wait,\n   })\n   ```\n   Plus a **terminal WARN** when the budget stops the bounded class (`Cause.done` path): `Effect.logWarning(\"retry budget exhausted\", { attempt, code, total POSTs: meta.attempt + 1 })`. This makes the chain observable even if the existing `llm.ts:283` `Effect.logError(\"stream error\")` bridge output is suppressed (the unexplained #144 zero-ERROR gap); the *acceptance criterion is grep-asserted* (§7 test 13), not assumed.\n2. **Error-class-scoped budget (B3) — replace blanket `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3`.** In `policy()`, after `retryable()` returns non-null:\n   - **Bounded class = timeout/stream-class** — `metadata.code` ∈ { `ProviderResponseStreamError`, `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError`, `ECONNRESET` }: tight retry cap `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES = 2` (retry count). Stop when `meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_RETRIES` → `Cause.done(meta.attempt)` (identical mechanism to the existing non-retryable stop, retry.ts:185).\n   - **Unbounded class = everything else**, in particular 429/usage-limit (`FreeUsageLimitError` / `GoUsageLimitError` — `retryable()` builds first-class upsell payloads, retry.ts:76–121), rate-limit text patterns, and 5xx: **preserve current retry-after honoring** (verified retry.ts `delay()` honors `retry-after-ms`/`retry-after` seconds/HTTP-date, caps only at `RETRY_MAX_DELAY`; upstream `retry.test.ts` \"uses retry-after values even when exceeding 10 minutes with headers\" is deliberate). A blanket attempt cap would convert \"wait out the 3-hour limit and continue\" into \"hard-fail after ~6 s\" — a serious self-inflicted availability regression on long agent runs.\n   - **Total-elapsed-retry-time budget**: for the bounded class an implicit ceiling already exists — `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES × (bodyIdleTimeout + backoff)` ≈ 2 × 10 min + 6 s < 25 min to terminal ERROR (§3.3). For the rate-limit class, **no** blanket elapsed budget — the deliberate semantics are \"wait out the limit\"; imposing one would regress the documented hours-long reset case. (Decided: no separate elapsed-budget primitive in this round; the attempt cap × idle deadline covers the hang class.)\n3. **Off-by-one fixed (R1)** — `meta.attempt` is 1-based retry count. `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES = 2` with stop at `meta.attempt > 2` ⇒ **initial + 2 retries = exactly 3 POSTs**. Invariant is stated and asserted in **POST counts** (server-side counter ≤ 3), never attempt indices. (The #175 formulation `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3` with `meta.attempt > 3` would have produced 4 POSTs — the exact off-by-one both r1 F9 and r3 R1 flagged.)\n4. **Second retry layer pinned (F9)** — `llm.ts:323` `maxRetries: input.retries ?? 0`: the AI-SDK layer retries only when `input.retries` is set. Assert `input.retries` is unset (0) for the hang path and count POSTs server-side, so the ≤3 invariant covers both layers.\n5. **Distinct error messages, shared class code** — `\"SSE read timed out\"` (chunkTimeout), `\"Body read timed out\"` (bodyIdleTimeout), `\"Body read deadline exceeded\"` (absolute cap), `\"Turn stalled...\"` (§5). All keep `metadata.code = \"ProviderResponseStreamError\"` so the bounded budget applies; the message discriminates for humans (r3 N5: a distinct code is possible but would require new `fromError` cases — decided: not worth the mapping churn this round; documented).\n6. **Relationship to #146** — with visible per-attempt WARN + terminal ERROR + budget, the #135/#146 watcher kill/restart remains the outer safety net for other failure modes; it is no longer the only recovery for this one.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Parsed-stream layer: turn-level guard + instrumentation (F5)\n\n### 5.1 The causal gap (r1 F5, the single most important gap)\n\nProduction `timeout: 3600000` (1 h) is a request-level `AbortSignal.timeout` that **does** fire on a stalled raw body (#145 proved it at 15 s in the harness). A raw-body stall bounded by a 1 h abort cannot produce the observed **10.9 h zero-retry zero-error** signature (#142/OZWZ). The production stall is therefore **above the raw-body layer**: `session/llm.ts:373` consumes the AI SDK's parsed `fullStream` via `Stream.fromAsyncIterable` with **no deadline of any kind** — precisely upstream issue #39968 (\"chunkTimeout only watches raw bytes, misses parsed-stream stalls\"). Every §6 raw-body test can pass while production still hangs at the parsed layer.\n\n### 5.2 Design (both halves)\n\n1. **Instrumentation (mandatory, minimal)**: at stream start in the `llm.ts` stream composition, log response metadata (content-type, transport, provider/model/session), and emit a per-parsed-event progress line (elapsed-since-last-parsed-event) at DEBUG. The real-provider capture (§7 test 15) then records the actual production content-type/transport/stall layer. This makes the *next* hang self-identifying.\n2. **Turn-level wall-clock guard (recommended)**: wrap the parsed-stream consumption with an idle-progress deadline:\n   ```ts\n   return Stream.fromAsyncIterable(result.result.fullStream, (e) => e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e))).pipe(\n     Stream.timeoutFail({\n       duration: Duration.millis(llmIdleTimeout),   // default 600_000, opt-in config\n       error: () => new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(`Turn stalled: no parsed stream event within ${llmIdleTimeout}ms`),\n     }),\n     Stream.mapEffect((event) => LLMAISDK.toLLMEvents(state, event)),\n     Stream.flatMap((events) => Stream.fromIterable(events)),\n   )\n   ```\n   `llmIdleTimeout` resets per *parsed* event (text delta, tool call, finish, …) and is opt-in (config `experimental.llmIdleTimeout`, or derived from `bodyIdleTimeout` when set). Because it throws `ResponseStreamError`, it flows into the same bounded retry budget (§4) — the raw-body deadline and the parsed-stream deadline are one coherent idle-progress policy across layers. This is the reconciliation the reviewers required: *any* stalled layer is now bounded, and the harness gains a parsed-stream stall test (below) that does not rely on the raw-body layer.\n3. **Scope note (r1)**: the binary contains a third transport — `packages/opencode/src/plugin/openai/ws.ts` (WebSocket Responses) with its own `idleTimeout`. It is OpenAI-plugin-scoped and not on our `opencode-go` path; documented as out of scope, re-checked on rebase. The v2 `LLMClient` transport (runner path) is separate; the guard here covers the v1 AI-SDK path that `opencode run` uses today.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Rebuild / replace / rollback (F10–F12)\n\n### 6.0 Step 0 — interim mitigation status (F13)\n\n`autoupdate: false` is **already set** and the #179 byte patch is **already applied** to both guard copies of the 1.18.13 binary (verified §0). Implementation step 0 is therefore: **re-verify the stopgap is still in place before and while building the fork** (a manual npm upgrade would wipe it), and keep it in place until the fork binary is live. If a wipe is detected, re-apply the #145 procedure (same-length replacement at the two shifted offsets, backup, atomic mv) per #179.\n\n### 6.1 Build prereqs (F11 — corrected)\n\n```bash\n# 1. bun, PINNED to the repo's packageManager (root package.json: \"bun@1.3.14\";\n#    packages/opencode/script/build.ts imports script/script.ts which enforces ^1.3.14)\n#    Install bun-v1.3.14 explicitly (NOT \"latest\").\ncurl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash -s -- bun-v1.3.14    # verify exact pin flag at implementation\n\n# 2. clone fork (canonical upstream, pinned tag) and apply the patch\ngit clone https://github.com/<org>/opencode-fork.git\ncd opencode-fork && git checkout v1.18.13 && git apply opencode-154-durable.patch\n\n# 3. install at the WORKSPACE ROOT (root package.json declares workspaces; root\n#    postinstall runs `bun run --cwd packages/core fix-node-pty`)\nbun install                                    # at repo root, NOT inside packages/opencode\n\n# 4. build single-target binary\ncd packages/opencode\nOPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.13-pp3g-fork OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g bun run build --single\n\n# 5. smoke test\n./dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode --version   # expect 1.18.13-pp3g-fork\n```\n\n- **`--skip-embed-web-ui` decision (F11)**: the fork **builds WITHOUT the flag first** (full fidelity: the embedded SolidJS web app). If the app build fails or is too slow, `--skip-embed-web-ui` is **accepted** — it degrades only the *embedded web dashboard* (`opencode serve`/web UI); the TUI and `opencode run` (the wrapper's launch path) are unaffected because the TUI ships in the main binary (`src/cli/tui/worker.ts`) and the web UI is a separate embedded bundle (`build.ts:26–50`). The decision taken is recorded in `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`.\n- **`bun install` must run at the root** — `build.ts`/`script.ts` assume the root install; the previous #175 instruction (\"cd packages/opencode; bun install\") would miss the root `postinstall` (`fix-node-pty`) and workspace resolution.\n\n### 6.2 Replace (F10 — truly atomic)\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup\n\n# backup current binary (stock 1.18.13, currently byte-patched)\ncp /home/claude-code/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.3/lib/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe \\\n   ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.stock-1.18.13\n\n# rotate previous fork binary\n[ -e ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe ] && \\\n  mv ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.previous\n\n# stage + same-filesystem atomic rename (the #145-proven pattern; NEVER cp over the live target)\ncp dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/.opencode.exe.new\nchmod +x ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/.opencode.exe.new\nmv ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/.opencode.exe.new ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\n# optional: fsync ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin before the rename if the fs demands it (r2)\n\n# point the wrapper at the fork binary; disable self-update is already in place\n# ~/.local/bin/opencode: REAL=\"$HOME/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\"\n```\n\nVerification after swap: `opencode --version` = `1.18.13-pp3g-fork`; `opencode models` works (wrapper models-cache rewrite); harness §7 green.\n\n### 6.3 Rollback\n\n```bash\n# restore the stock binary to the fork path, or flip wrapper REAL back to the nvm symlink\ncp ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.stock-1.18.13 ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/.opencode.exe.new\nmv ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/.opencode.exe.new ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe   # atomic same-fs\n# or: sed -i 's#REAL=.*#REAL=\"<nvm symlink>\"#' ~/.local/bin/opencode\nopencode --version   # confirm\n```\n\nRollback criterion: any provider regression (e.g., legitimate non-SSE bodies aborting, or the parsed-stream guard false-firing) → restore stock and report; the #146 watcher remains the safety net meanwhile.\n\n### 6.4 Fork-identity marker + drift detection (F12)\n\n- **Marker (nearly free)**: `build.ts:192–199` defines `OPENCODE_VERSION` / `OPENCODE_CHANNEL` from env; `packages/core/src/installation/version.ts` reads them (`InstallationVersion = OPENCODE_VERSION`), and `opencode --version` reports them. Build with `OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.13-pp3g-fork OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g` ⇒ the binary is **indistinguishable-from-stock problem solved** — `--version` shows the fork marker.\n- **Runtime string marker**: the patched binary embeds `\"Body read timed out\"` (and, while the interim patch is in place, the `/*XXX…*/` filler) — greppable for presence checks independent of the version string.\n- **Launch-time drift detection**: modify `~/.local/bin/opencode` — before `exec \"$REAL\" \"$@\"`, run `\"$REAL\" --version` and assert the fork marker; on mismatch, print a loud error to stderr and `exit 1` (do **not** silently launch stock). This turns the 03:15-style silent wipe into a hard, operator-visible failure.\n- **Watcher drift check**: add the same marker assertion to the #146 watcher's periodic check so non-wrapper launches are covered too.\n\n### 6.5 Documentation + rebase discipline\n\n`.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md` (mirrors `crosslink-fork.md`): upstream identity, pinned tag, both patches (§2.2/§2.3), build/replace/rollback commands, marker + drift-check procedure, and the invariant \"any upgrade = rebuild the fork at the new tag and re-apply both patches\". Rebase checklist: (a) `provider.ts` + `aiskd.ts` content-type guard count = 0 each; (b) `wrapBodyIdle` marker present in both; (c) fork `--version` marker present; (d) §7 unit tests green; (e) re-verify the v2 reachability assumption (§2.1).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Verification matrix (R2, R3, and additions)\n\n### 7.1 Harness reuse + new modes\n\nReuse `/tmp/opencode-hang-test/` (`server.js` modes 0/1/2, `cfg/opencode.json` with `chunkTimeout: 3000`, `headerTimeout: 2000`, `timeout: 15000`). Add to `cfg`: `bodyIdleTimeout: 30000` (and `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` for the tests that need it). Add to `server.js`:\n\n- `SLOW_CHUNK_MS` env — write chunks with inter-chunk delays (test 6).\n- `PER_REQUEST` mode — differentiate per request: request #1 hangs, request #2 healthy (R3, test 7).\n- `GZIP` env — gzip-encode the non-SSE body with `Content-Encoding: gzip` (F8, test 10).\n- `STALLED` mode — chunks every N min where N > idle threshold (test 9).\n- A parsed-stream stall mode for the turn-level guard (test 9b): a well-formed SSE stream whose *parsed* event cadence stops (raw chunks keep arriving or not — the guard fires on parsed-event idle).\n\n### 7.2 Matrix (patched fork binary)\n\n| # | Scenario | Parameters | Expected | Proves |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | application/json + hang | mode 1, ct=application/json | abort within `bodyIdleTimeout`; **≤3 POSTs**; grep-asserted **ERROR** line; error exit (not EXIT 124) | non-SSE hang killed; budget; error surfacing |\n| 2 | text/event-stream + hang | mode 1, ct=text/event-stream | abort within `chunkTimeout` (unchanged); ≤3 POSTs; ERROR | SSE path unchanged; budget |\n| 3 | no response at all | mode 0 | headerTimeout fires; 4 `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries | headerTimeout untouched |\n| 4 | healthy application/json | complete body | EXIT 0, no retries, no abort | no regression |\n| 5 | healthy text/event-stream | mode 2 | \"Hello world\", EXIT 0, no retries | no regression |\n| 6 | **slow-but-legit non-SSE (R2 — parameters FIXED)** | `SLOW_CHUNK_MS=5000`, 5 chunks, `chunkTimeout=3000`, `bodyIdleTimeout=30000` — **gaps (5 s) MUST exceed chunkTimeout (3 s)** | completes, EXIT 0, no abort | hy3 F2 preserved; discriminates A' from A (gap > chunkTimeout ⇒ Option A would false-abort) |\n| 6b | slow-but-legit non-SSE, never completes | same server minus final chunk | aborts at `bodyIdleTimeout` (≤ ~30 s) | non-SSE deadline kills dead bodies (R2 variant) |\n| 7 | **per-request abort (R3)** | `PER_REQUEST` mode: req 1 hangs/aborts, req 2 healthy | healthy completes unaffected; aborted request's signal/reason isolated | hy3 F4 — controller per-request. Source-confirmed downgrade documented: `provider.ts:1746` constructs `new AbortController()` inside the per-call fetch closure (only the SDK instance is memoised); the concurrency test is a regression guard, not the primary proof |\n| 8 | bodyIdleTimeout sensitivity | 2000 vs 4000 | retry cadence tracks the knob | mechanism is the config knob |\n| 9 | **stalled-but-not-dead stream (F.1)** | chunks every 15 min, `bodyIdleTimeout=600000`, absolute unset | aborts at `bodyIdleTimeout` (10 min) — NOT at any total cap | discriminates A' (idle fires) from B (would wait for total); the test r1 said \"would have surfaced B2\" |\n| 9b | **parsed-stream stall (F5)** | SSE mode, raw bytes fine, parsed events stop | turn-level guard fires `ResponseStreamError(\"Turn stalled...\")`; ≤3 POSTs; ERROR | the production layer #39968 — the raw-body tests cannot see it |\n| 10 | **gzip non-SSE body (F8)** | `GZIP` healthy + `GZIP` hang | healthy completes without double-decode/length error; hang aborts within `bodyIdleTimeout` | compressed bodies safe under the wrapper |\n| 11 | **non-chat request (F8)** | non-chat endpoint (e.g., models list / token count) with non-SSE content-type | passes through; when `bodyIdleTimeout` unconfigured → unwrapped (opt-in semantics); when configured → completes correctly | opt-in wrapping doesn't break non-chat traffic |\n| 12 | **fork unit tests (F.4)** | `packages/opencode/test/session/retry.test.ts` + provider wrapper tests | see 7.3 | divergence protected across upstream rebases |\n| 13 | **grep-assert ERROR (F4)** | after each hang test | `grep` the run log: ≥1 `level=ERROR` line + per-attempt `level=WARN message=\"retry\"` lines + terminal budget-exhausted WARN | error visibility is an assertable criterion, not an eyeballed expectation |\n| 14 | **POST counts, not attempt indices (F9/R1)** | server-side counter | ≤3 POSTs for hang scenarios | invariant in the observable quantity |\n| 15 | **real-provider capture (F5)** | one instrumented `opencode run` against real `opencode-go` | records content-type/transport/last-progress; no regression on a normal call | identifies the production stall layer; exercises the instrumentation |\n\n### 7.3 Fork unit tests (r1 F.4 / r2 / r3)\n\nIn `packages/opencode/test/session/retry.test.ts` (already exists, verified):\n1. Bounded-class cap: `ResponseStreamError`-coded error retried at attempts 1 and 2, `Cause.done` at attempt 3 (⇒ 3 POSTs total) — assert the `policy` step returns done after `meta.attempt > 2`.\n2. Unbounded-class preserved: 429 `retry-after` error still honors the header (existing \"exceeding 10 minutes\" test must still pass unchanged).\n3. Off-by-one regression: delay sequence `[2000, 4000]` then stop for the bounded class.\n4. Per-attempt logging: the `policy` step emits a WARN per attempt with attempt/code/nextDelay (assert via a captured Effect logger or by asserting the `set` payload contract).\n5. `wrapBodyIdle` (provider wrapper tests): idle fires on gap > ms; slow progress (gaps < ms) does not fire; `done`/`cancel` clear the timer; the absolute cap fires only when configured; dispatcher routes SSE → `wrapSSE`, non-SSE → `wrapBodyIdle`, unconfigured → unwrapped; absent content-type → non-SSE branch (r2).\n\n### 7.4 r2's additional required checks\n\n- **Wrapper survival test**: flip `REAL` to the fork path, simulate an npm upgrade of the stock package, assert the wrapper still resolves the fork binary and `autoupdate: false` is effective (r2 #3).\n- **Consumer cancellation test**: cancel the consuming stream mid-body; assert the wrapper's reader is cancelled and timers cleared (r2 #5).\n- **Exit-code verification**: assert `opencode run`'s non-zero/error completion on session error (r3 N4 — currently an assumption).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Change-log vs #175\n\n| #175 | Revised (#180) | Reviewer driver |\n|---|---|---|\n| §0 \"installed = 1.18.12, patch wiped\" | installed = **1.18.13**, #179 stopgap **re-applied** (both copies byte-patched), `autoupdate:false` **set**; urgency reframed: box protected but ephemeral | live re-verification |\n| §1 fork pin v1.18.12 | pin **installed version at implementation time** (today 1.18.13); re-verify byte-identity incl. `aiskd.ts` | F11 / live state |\n| §2 patch provider.ts only | **patch BOTH** `provider.ts` + `aiskd.ts` (dispatcher + `wrapBodyIdle`); reachability evidence + rebase re-check | **B1** |\n| §3 Option B total-completion deadline | **Option A'** idle-progress (`bodyIdleTimeout=600000`, opt-in `bodyAbsoluteTimeout=3300000` default OFF); numeric chain 30 min < 60 min < operator; Option B false-abort class documented | **B2** |\n| §4 blanket `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3` (off-by-one) | **error-class-scoped** `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2` (`meta.attempt > 2` ⇒ ≤3 POSTs); retry-after/429/usage-limit preserved; elapsed-budget decision | **B3**, **R1**, F9 |\n| §4 relies on `halt()` for visibility | **per-attempt WARN at retry boundary** + terminal budget-exhausted WARN + grep-asserted ERROR | **F4** |\n| (absent) | **turn-level parsed-stream guard** (`llm.ts` fullStream, `llmIdleTimeout`) + instrumentation + real-provider capture | **F5** |\n| `wrapBody` eager `start()` loop, unsound timer/controller | **pull() shape**, `settled` guard, `clearTimeout` in cancel, `.catch` on cancel promise | **F6**, **F7** |\n| `bodyTimeout` defaulted ON | **`bodyIdleTimeout` opt-in** (like `chunkTimeout`); gzip + non-chat tests | **F8** |\n| `meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (4 POSTs) + second retry layer unpinned | `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2`; **POST-count invariant**; `input.retries` pinned | **F9**, **R1** |\n| §5.2 `cp` over live target labelled \"atomic\" | **stage + same-fs `mv`** (with backup rotation + optional fsync); rollback uses the same atomic swap | **F10**, r2 #2 |\n| §5.1 `cd packages/opencode; bun install`, bun \"latest\", no web-UI decision | **workspace-root `bun install`**, **bun@1.3.14 pin**, **`--skip-embed-web-ui` decision documented**, root postinstall `fix-node-pty` | **F11** |\n| (absent) | **fork-identity marker** (`OPENCODE_VERSION`/`OPENCODE_CHANNEL` defines) + **launch-time drift detection** (wrapper + #146 watcher) + rebase re-check | **F12** |\n| (absent) | step 0: interim stopgap status documented (`autoupdate:false` set, #179 byte patch live) | **F13** |\n| §6 test 6 params contradictory (2 s < 3 s) | **test 6 gaps MUST exceed `chunkTimeout`** (5 s gaps × 5 chunks, `chunkTimeout=3000`, `bodyIdleTimeout=30000`) + never-completes variant | **R2** |\n| §6 test 7 underspecified (one mode for all requests) | **`PER_REQUEST` server mode** (req 1 hangs, req 2 healthy) + source-confirmed downgrade documented (`provider.ts:1746`) | **R3** |\n| matrix: 8 tests | + stalled-but-not-dead (9), parsed-stream stall (9b), gzip (10), non-chat (11), fork unit tests (12), grep-assert ERROR (13), POST counts (14), real-provider capture (15); absent-content-type + consumer-cancellation + wrapper-survival checks | F.1–F.5, r2 |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Open items / handoff\n\n- **Implementer**: build the fork @ installed version (today v1.18.13) with §2.2/§2.3 patches, §4 budget + logging, §5 guard; run §7 matrix incl. unit tests; install per §6.2; write `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`; keep step-0 stopgap verified.\n- **Reviewer**: assess against §7 matrix and the three verdicts (B1–B3, F4–F13, R1–R3).\n- **Upstream tra